; measured turnover at the prescribed 5000 half-window peaks at only 0.286 with 33 shared contacts. What changes is which group member serves as hub (121/357 early, 1415 mid, 1460/1701/1923 late), which makes raw edge-set diffs look disjoint (jaccard 0.0) even though neighbour identities are unchanged. Group degree and event volume are flat with zero detected bursts, and the one large turnover spike at bandwidth 2500 aligns exactly with an empty activity bin, marking it a sparse-sampling artifact rather than a transition."}, "raw_final_response": "## Conclusion\n\n**The apparent \"change\" is a hub rotation within a fixed contact pool, not a regime switch.**\n\nKey findings:\n\n1. **The external contact set is essentially constant.** Node 121's partners in [64269,74269] (step_07) and node 1701's partners in [86269,94269] (step_08) are the *same ~30 nodes* (170, 172, 195, 272, 309, 324, 325, 337, 426, 460, 462, 474, 519, 593, 694, 834, 901, 922, 932, 1044, 1091, 1105, 1154, 1416, 1437, 1520, 1619, 1635, 1743, 1897), differing only by singletons (1622 vs. 235). Node 1415 in the middle period (step_10) contacts that identical set.\n\n2. **What rotates is which group member is the active hub.** Early: 121 and 357 carry 90 events each while 1460/1701/1923 are silent (step_05). Late: 1460/1701/1923 carry 34/91/90 events while 121/357 drop to 1\u20132 (step_06). Group degree stays flat at 32\u201339 throughout (step_09).\n\n3. **The \"jaccard 0.0\" in step_04 is an artifact of edge-identity**: the *endpoints* changed (121\u2192170 became 1701\u2192170) while the neighbor identities did not. The proper turnover measure at the prescribed 5000 half-window peaks at only **0.286** (step_01), with before/after sets sharing 33 of ~39 contacts \u2014 ordinary background churn.\n\n4. **Confounder controls**: no activity bursts at all (step_12, 0 bursts, flat ~73 events/bin); the 0.7 spike at bandwidth 2500 (step_11, t=78307) coincides exactly with the empty bin 78269\u201380268 (step_02, value 0), i.e. a sampling artifact of a quiet stretch, and it reverts to 0.03 immediately after. Late-window connectivity (step_13) is a pre-existing edge, not a new partner.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_25544f86\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [121, 357, 381, 594, 728, 785, 898, 1269, 1415, 1460, 1701, 1923],\n  \"window\": [64269, 94269],\n  \"confidence\": 0.85,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"No abrupt partner substitution. The group's external neighbourhood is a stable pool of ~30 nodes present from the start to the end of the window; measured turnover at the prescribed 5000 half-window peaks at only 0.286 with 33 shared contacts. What changes is which group member serves as hub (121/357 early, 1415 mid, 1460/1701/1923 late), which makes raw edge-set diffs look disjoint (jaccard 0.0) even though neighbour identities are unchanged. Group degree and event volume are flat with zero detected bursts, and the one large turnover spike at bandwidth 2500 aligns exactly with an empty activity bin, marking it a sparse-sampling artifact rather than a transition.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 60182, "total_output_tokens": 5272, "total_tokens": 65454, "total_latency_ms": 76954, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}